  "notes": "Original native GLSL preserves the cell grid, gap, three alpha masks, HSL transformations, color cycling and eleven-stop moving gradient. The 12-direction Perlin-family gradient noise uses a reproducible integer hash instead of the browser random permutation seed, so the random field realization differs. State advances at a normalized 60 Hz reference; it is not claimed pixel-identical to a random browser run."
